   "source": [
    "### Q7: What is the benefit of using a multivariate control chart over several separate univariate control charts? What is one limitation?"
   ]
  },A multivariate control chart monitors several related variables at the same time while accounting for correlations between them. This can help identify unusual patterns that separate univariate charts might miss. One limitation is that a multivariate chart does not automatically identify which variable caused an out-of-control signal, so additional analysis may be needed.
